WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.970
Panda Corner Contest!

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.190
That would be a mandrill.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.450
That would be Tandoori.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.750
That would be the 
Awa Dance <i>(Awa Odori)</i>.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.830
We're talking about a 
slump <i>(kankodori)</i>.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.840
So why is the Panda Corner in a slump?

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.930
The Penguin Action Hero 
Show took our visitors.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.560
Gentooger!

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:21.870
Chinstrapger!

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.840
Adélienger!

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.800
South Pole Squad

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.820
Penguinger!

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.000
Wow, it must be doing very well.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.370
But don't you think it's 
missing something?

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:51.980
You think so?

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:52.970
For example,

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:55.600
I think it'd be even more popular

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.650
if they had a more 
 well-known penguin in it.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:02:59.990
You're right.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.750
Like a Northern Rockhopper Penguin.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.330
Why can't you just be 
a little more sincere?

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.150
Do you want to be in the show?

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.970
Well, not really.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.720
But don't you think it'd do better with

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.010
some traditional comedic storytelling?

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:17.800
That would be rather dull.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.420
How about listening for yourself
 if it's dull or not?

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:23.810
Pardon me, could we order now?

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:24.600
Certainly!

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.840
Sorry, I'm a little busy right now.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.560
So please think of this as me.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:35.500
You know, I'm not so bored that I can

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.020
tell comedic stories to a clay statue.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:39.530
I'll be right with you!

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:44.180
Come on, listen to me!

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:45.260
Oh, sorry.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:46.780
What were we talking about?

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:50.220
The Panda Corner is boring!

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:52.510
It's already boring to begin with,

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:55.040
and now there aren't any visitors!

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.790
I can't deal with this.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.160
But Mr. Handa was mentioning how

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.800
the show brought in more visitors

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.640
and was rather happy about it.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.180
Really?

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:10.020
Well... it doesn't really concern me.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:14.970
How about you work harder to 
make the zoo exciting, Panda?

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:18.170
I wonder if I can do it...

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.570
Lack of confidence?

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.640
That's rare for you, Panda.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.540
What's that?

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.450
It's hot ginger.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.920
It smells really good.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.380
I made it from homemade ginger syrup.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.330
Drink it and feel better.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:45.790
Thank you.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.350
Hot ginger is delicious.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.310
Ginger?

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.560
That would be danger.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.010
That would be a rice 
cooker <i>(suihanjaa)</i>.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.410
This is hot ginger!

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:11.410
And what's popular is Penguinger.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.800
So bored...

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.180
I'm catching up with my side job.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.840
So bored!

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:32.600
Then will you help me 
with my side job?

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.930
Well, let me think...

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.480
Nah, that's okay.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.700
Oh, I see...

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.960
So bored.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:54.910
Panda! Thanks for your hard work!

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.460
Panda!

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.050
Could it be you're depressed

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:04.030
since the Panda Corner's popularity has slipped?

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.760
How did you guess?

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.540
It's obvious.

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:17.630
It's none of your business, Rin Rin!

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:19.480
Hey, wait!

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.690
I might be able to help somehow.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.410
Because you know, 
if you're sad,

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.990
then I get sad, too.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:45.920
I wonder how we can 
get more visitors...

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:49.510
How about a photo contest?

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.830
A photo conte—

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.520
See? Like this.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:00.280
If you hold a photo contest,

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:01.870
you're bound to get visitors.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.110
That might be a good idea.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:08.490
The one voted most popular 
will get the grand pri—

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.940
We don't have any money to spend.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:14.270
There's no way we could 
afford a fancy prize.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.900
It's a prize that won't require money.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:17.910
What?

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:20.540
The chance to spend a whole 
day playing with Panda.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.880
<i>Mr. Panda!</i>

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:25.730
What do you think?

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:28.050
Then you won't have 
to spend any money.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:32.000
I think that might be a great idea!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:32.680
Right?

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.850
I can get lots of pictures 
taken of me...

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.310
...and the contest will be a big hit.

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:43.270
And the Panda Corner will 
be full of visitors!

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:48.990
I'll go talk to Mr. Handa about it.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:50.400
Hey, Panda!

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:55.280
Rin Rin...

00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:59.070
Thank you.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.740
Okay, bye-bye.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:12.880
There's no doubt about it. 
Panda is so cute!

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:18.160
I'm going to win the grand prize 
in that photo contest!

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:29.480
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:36.890
Coffee Roaster Masaki

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:36.930
Coffee Roaster...

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:38.690
Masaki!

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.060
My name is Masaki.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.730
I'm currently an apprentice under

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:45.960
Mr. Tree Kangaroo to 
become a coffee roaster.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:53.800
Handpicking day after day...

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.800
I want to start roasting already.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.970
Masaki.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.010
Move your hands, not your mouth.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:01.220
Okay...

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.070
That smells so great.

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.310
Master, you're awesome!

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:19.660
I want to roast beans as soon as possible!

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:23.250
You want to try?

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:24.660
Huh?

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:24.660
Huh?

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.830
You mean I can roast?!

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:29.410
However, you'll roast the beans that

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:30.880
didn't pass the handpicking.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:36.510
Oh, so first I'll practice 
with the rejected beans.

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:38.360
All right!

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:40.300
I totally know how to use that

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.850
machine after watching you every day!

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:44.980
You won't be using the roasting machine.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.420
Huh?

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.930
This is so lame.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.030
Beginners have to start with that.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.420
Come on now. Make sure you 
stir them properly.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.790
If you don't, some of 
the beans will burn.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:09.180
Shut up...

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:14.130
Hey! It's starting to smell good!

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.170
How's that look?

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:18.780
It doesn't look that different 
from the good beans.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:23.540
Oh my, it's roasted nicely 
through the middle.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.850
Not bad for your first try.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.060
You're right.

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:31.160
All right. Since it looks 
good, let's try it!

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:39.720
All right. Now to drip brew 
some in my cu—

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:43.130
One, two, one, two, there we go.

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:47.580
Masaki, I'd like mine at about 
42 degrees so it's plenty hot.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.510
It's not a bath!

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:55.340
And the Masaki coffee is complete!

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.130
Huh?

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:02.940
It smells sort of weird.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:09.180
S-So gross...

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:13.490
I was completely deceived by the

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:15.400
really good smell when it was roasting.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.120
See? Do you get it now?

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:23.370
You get terrible tasting coffee 
when moldy beans get mixed in.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.380
And when you roast them,

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:28.450
you can't really tell them 
apart just by looking.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.370
So, mediocre coffee shops

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.540
sometimes don't know the value of handpicking.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:37.530
Master, that was mean!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.720
Did you know this would 
happen from the start?

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:45.910
Now you know personally

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:47.510
how important the raw materials are.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:49.490
Well, yeah...

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.850
So the reason 
Tree Kangaroo Coffee is good

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:57.440
is because all of you work so hard.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.440
Master...

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.070
I'll continue to do my best!

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:09.310
Well, then here's your 
batch for today.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:22.970
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:27.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:26.600
Panda Corner Project!

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:30.320
Mr. Panda!

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.190
Service, service.

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.440
Looks like the photo 
contest is going great.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:40.300
Service, service!

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.550
Service, service!

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:45.350
The grand prize is going to be mine!

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:53.000
The Penguin Action Hero Show
will be starting momentarily.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.290
Service, service.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:03.540
Huh?!

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.470
Llamaranger!

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:28.930
Well, now it's time for the side job.

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:31.660
South Pole Squad

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:32.870
Penguinger!

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.290
Adélien Kick!

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:40.460
Gentoo Flipper!

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:42.670
Chinstrap Beam!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.690
The islands of the South Pole

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:50.300
will never fall into your 
hands as long as we're here!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.220
Penguinger!

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:02.520
The battle is not yet 
over, Penguingers.

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:04.440
That voice!

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:07.360
I am the one who freezes 
the white South Pole

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.470
with a dark, black blizzard.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:13.370
The one with the cold 
heart of -60 degrees.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:16.200
The ruler of the South Pole...

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.830
Emperor Penguin!

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:21.590
The evil emperor!

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:25.290
Penguingers,

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.350
listen to the comedic 
storytelling of doom!

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.720
Cover your ears!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.870
If you hear it, you'll be 
turned into plushies!

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.010
What?!

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:37.590
Well, let's start off with 
a slightly idiotic tale.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:42.390
The things I'm scared of are manju.

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:44.290
What kind of bugs are manju?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.530
They aren't bugs...

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.360
So in the end...

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.830
Did you just want to be in 
the show, Mr. Penguin?

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.960
What are you talking 
about, Miss Sasako?

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.040
Actually, I didn't have much of a choice.

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:01.640
You just wanted to be in it.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:05.380
Yes, that's right. I'm sorry.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:07.580
Must be nice.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:11.070
All of the visitors that were 
doing the photo contest

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:14.610
went over to the Penguinger show.

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:18.140
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.690
Do you have any better ideas?

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:23.650
Well, let's see...

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.320
How about this?

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.360
What, what?

00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:41.040
The Panda Family will be performed 
in the Panda Corner momentarily.

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:49.660
This is an ordinary tale 
about an ordinary family

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:51.840
that lives in an ordinary town.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.400
The only unusual thing about them

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:58.320
is that they're a family of pandas.

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:05.440
Darling, could you not read 
the paper while we're eating?

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:11.650
Mom, I want some bread.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.560
What are you talking about?

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:16.120
You're a panda, so you'll
 eat bamboo grass.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:21.530
And, Grandpa, no doing 
tai chi while you're eating.

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:23.570
A balanced diet leads 
to a healthy body.

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:26.130
Can I get some more bamboo grass, Mom?

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:28.300
Oh, all right.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:33.020
More importantly, what are you 
going to do about your future?

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:36.710
All you do is lay around all day.

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:40.390
I don't lay around.
 I laze around.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:44.750
You should be able to tell 
the difference by now.

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:51.780
Don't suck me up!

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:54.340
Darling, put down the paper.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:01.500
Don't suck me up!

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:08.130
Oh?

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:10.800
Oh, one second.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.370
Hello?

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:19.600
What? Our missing eldest 
son has been found?

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:21.230
What?

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:23.520
Our brother Stojković?

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:30.480
I'm home!

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:33.790
Oh, Stojković!

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:36.780
Look how much you've grown.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:38.450
I'm sorry, Mom.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:42.410
Darling, look, it's Stojković!

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:47.420
I thought I told you

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:51.250
when you rushed out that 
door to never come back.

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:54.290
I'm sorry, Dad.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:57.340
I'll carry on the family 
business after all.

00:17:57.980 --> 00:18:00.230
You will, Stojković?

00:17:57.980 --> 00:18:00.760
Smooth sailing.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.090
Are you sure?

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:05.180
You ran away because you didn't 
like the family business.

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:05.180
Indulging in every possible luxury.

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:08.800
After seeing this vast world,

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:10.930
I realized that I was only concerned

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:12.650
with the small meaningless things.

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:14.990
Stojković...

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:20.030
I'll be the best flatus patsy ever, Dad.

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:23.910
Happy family gathering.

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:24.950
Thank you, Stojković.

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:26.660
Happy family gathering.

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:28.020
What's a flatus patsy?

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.700
Fried salmon lunch.

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:32.170
It's not a job for a guy.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:34.250
There's a bath ready for you.

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:35.700
One-plate meal.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.720
Go wash off the years of dirt.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:38.560
Okay.

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:47.060
All better.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.480
What?!

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:53.420
Brother, you're not a panda?

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:54.140
First and probably the last.

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:55.440
What's going on?

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:00.410
Well, you see, 
Stojković is a polar bear.

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:03.620
What?! A polar bear?

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:07.200
I never realized.

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.780
A bolt out of the blue!

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.820
Since we're already disclosing...

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:16.490
I'm actually not your older brother.

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:18.010
I'm your older sister.

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:21.640
What?! Older sister?

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:27.700
Sorry. We were going 
to tell you one day.

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.310
Sorry, you two.

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:35.650
Brother! I mean... Sister?

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.280
What's wrong?

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:39.950
I-I'm giving birth!

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:49.790
What?! A penguin?!

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.920
Good boy.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.800
It's the start of a new family.

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:59.310
Why's it a penguin?

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:01.890
These are such hard times that

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:04.440
even families may not 
understand each other.

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:07.600
I think it's all right 
for a family like this

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:11.270
to exist in this vast world.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:12.950
Yeah.

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:15.650
You're right.

00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:24.600
Happily ever after!

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.910
Reserved for a 
Private Event Today

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:34.940
The Panda Corner project 
was a huge success!

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:38.380
Thanks to my passionate role as the baby.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:41.760
I heard it was really popular.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.720
Congratulations, Panda.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:45.730
Yeah!

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:49.220
And we're going to have 
an encore performance!

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.890
Thank you for all your 
hard work, everyone.

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:54.690
Here you go.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:58.760
Wow it looks so good!

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:00.320
Oh, you shouldn't have.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:05.000
Hey, how about we put my 
comedic storytelling in the play?

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.840
Nah, that's okay.

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:08.970
Why, Panda?

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:11.150
Have you even heard my 
comedic storytelling before?

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:13.720
I don't have to.

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:17.740
Registered mail.

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:19.290
Coming.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:27.220
Mr. Rintarou Hayashi
In the 1st ever Panda Corner Photo Contest,

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:27.220
Ticket to Play with 
Pandas for a Day

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:33.430
Yeah! I got the grand prize 
in the photo contest!

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:37.440
Panda!

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:39.900
Let's play!

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:44.110
I was waiting for you, Hayashi.

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:52.490
Now then, let's play.

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:55.550
This is a brand new game where we both

00:21:55.550 --> 00:21:59.980
put these ads into these tissue packs.

00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:03.260
What do you think? Sounds fun, right?

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:07.000
Here's your stack, Hayashi.

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:10.650
Let's have a fun day together.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:12.190
Right.

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:24.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:22.770
Next Time

00:23:58.140 --> 00:23:59.830
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:00.910
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:02.330
Have you ever donated blood?

00:24:02.330 --> 00:24:03.040
I have.

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:05.090
I'm changing the subject now.

00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:07.410
You're changing the subject? 
Well, whatever.

00:24:07.410 --> 00:24:10.440
I want someone to make a 
fuss over me very quickly.

00:24:10.440 --> 00:24:11.860
Do I qualify?

00:24:11.860 --> 00:24:14.050
I think you're super cute, Panda.

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:14.970
I knew it.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:16.260
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:17.850
Next week's Polar Bear Café...

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:19.730
If you get it in your eyes, 
please don't rub them

00:24:19.620 --> 00:24:22.770
Wolf's Occupation Change
Mr Penguin's New Love

00:24:19.730 --> 00:24:21.200
and gently rinse with water.

00:24:21.200 --> 00:24:22.770
Exactly what did you 
end up explaining?

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:24.040
Please take care!

